[PERFORMANCE & ASYNCHRONOUS SCALING MANDATE]
1. ZERO BLOCKING I/O IN HTTP REQUESTS:
   - ALL network I/O, external HTTP calls (Chapa API, SMS Gateways, Email, S3/Cloudinary media processing) MUST run inside Celery tasks (task.delay()).
   - The Django request-response cycle must return under 100ms.

2. REDIS CACHING & FAST DATA PATTERNS:
   - Dynamic settings, category trees, and frequently accessed storefront queries must be cached in Redis with graceful cache-aside patterns.
   - High-velocity, temporary data (Shopping Carts, 15-minute Checkout Stock Locks, Rate Limiting, Delivery OTP verification attempts) MUST live primarily in Redis, using PostgreSQL only as a persistent fallback.

3. CELERY BACKGROUND WORKERS & PERIODIC BEAT:
   - Payout reconciliations, trust-tier metrics recalculation, expired stock reservation cleanup, and 72-hour escrow release checks MUST run as scheduled Celery Beat jobs.
   - All tasks must be idempotent, accepting UUIDs/IDs instead of serialized model instances.